{
  "_README": "#5079 (epic #5051, charter #5067): the FIXED training scorecard the /training-review block retro re-grades once per block (the block is the charter's rotation.anchors_fixed_weeks; the retro cadence is the charter's calibration.block_retro). Thirteen rows, copied from the owner-private elite-panel review of 2026-10-18 (the rows and their baseline grades only; the review itself stays private). Each row names the platform reads that grade it (`inputs`, keys of lambdas/training/block_retro.py's evidence) and, where code can score it, its `code_rules` (ADR-105: deterministic computation before any model verdict); the eight-seat panel re-grade (route charter.retro, one call per seat) scores every row, and lambdas/training/block_retro.py combines the two. Every training TARGET is read from config/training_charter.json at run time, never copied here. Hand-owned; a change is a new version with a change_log line. A grade below `grade_scale.fix_below` becomes a named fix (an issue or a charter change for the owner).",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "change_log": [
    {"version": "1.0.0", "date": "2026-10-19", "issue": "#5079", "what": "the thirteen rows of the 2026-10-18 elite-panel review, their measurable inputs, the code rules, the grade scale and the baseline grades"}
  ],
  "grade_scale": {
    "score_range": [0, 10],
    "rule": "a row score is 0-10; the letter is the highest row whose `min` the score reaches. The scale refines config/panel_rubric.json's letters (A, A-, B+ share their floors; B, C and D are each split into a plus/plain/minus band inside the rubric's own band), so a row score and a panel seat score read on one scale. tests/test_block_retro_5079.py holds the refinement.",
    "letters": [
      {"letter": "A", "min": 9.0},
      {"letter": "A-", "min": 8.5},
      {"letter": "B+", "min": 8.0},
      {"letter": "B", "min": 7.5},
      {"letter": "B-", "min": 7.0},
      {"letter": "C+", "min": 6.5},
      {"letter": "C", "min": 6.0},
      {"letter": "D+", "min": 5.5},
      {"letter": "D", "min": 5.0},
      {"letter": "F", "min": 0.0}
    ],
    "fix_below": "B"
  },
  "combine_rule": "a row's score is the mean of its code score (the mean of its measured code_rules) and the panel's median seat score; with only one of the two it is that one; with neither the row is `ungraded` and carries its last grade, said so. The session may override a row only with a recorded reason (block_retro.apply_overrides).",
